1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:09,300
No -b:a. What bitrate do you get?

2
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:16,760
Mono and stereo, four sample rates.

3
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:23,830
Synthetic pink noise, 10 seconds.

4
00:00:23,830 --> 00:00:32,310
Two readers: declared, and packet sizes.

5
00:00:32,310 --> 00:00:38,230
Stereo: about 128 kbps, every rate.

6
00:00:38,230 --> 00:00:43,160
Both readers agree within 1%.

7
00:00:43,160 --> 00:00:47,140
Mono: about 69 kbps.

8
00:00:47,140 --> 00:00:53,110
Not 64. Not half of stereo.

9
00:00:53,110 --> 00:00:58,040
Silence: about 2 kbps.

10
00:00:58,040 --> 00:01:09,140
Control: MP3 is a fixed 128 / 64 kbps.

11
00:01:09,140 --> 00:01:14,390
-b:a 96k gives 96 kbps.

12
00:01:14,390 --> 00:01:20,700
If the number matters, set it.

13
00:01:20,700 --> 00:01:25,490
Default: ~128 stereo, ~69 mono.

14
00:01:25,490 --> 00:01:31,240
Not tested: real music, VBR, 5.1.
